Imagine that China is like a really, really big school with lots and lots of classrooms.

In your school in London, you have a Head Teacher who makes the big rules, right? Well, China has a big group of people called the **National People’s Congress**. You can think of them like the **Big School Council**.

Here is what they do:

1.  **They make the rules:** Just like your class might decide, "No running in the hallway," the National People’s Congress decides the big rules for the whole country. These rules help everyone know how to behave and stay safe.
2.  **They pick the helpers:** They choose the people who will be the "Head Teachers" and "Class Monitors" for the country. These helpers are the ones who do the everyday jobs, like building roads, making sure schools are open, and helping people when they are sick.
3.  **They listen to ideas:** Lots of people from all over China send their best helpers to this big meeting. They talk about what the country needs, like more parks or better hospitals, and then they decide together what to do.

So, the National People’s Congress is like the biggest meeting in China where important people come together to make the rules and choose the leaders who take care of everyone. It’s a bit like when all the teachers and parents in your school meet to decide how to make the school a happy and safe place for you! 🏫🇨🇳 [end of text]


